 "fabric": {
  "title": "Rayon",
  "text": "Rayon, also called viscose, is a semi-synthetic fiber made from natural sources of regenerated cellulose, such as wood and related agricultural products. It has the same molecular structure as cellulose. Many types and grades of rayon fibers and films exist. Some imitate the feel and texture of natural fibers such as silk, wool, cotton, and linen.",
  "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rayon",
